zune-jpeg: keep the multi-scan baseline mode when a later component scan resumes

`decode_mcu_ycbcr_baseline_inner` (mcu.rs) decides between row-by-row output
and buffering every component scan for the whole image (multi-SOS images
whose first scan lacks some components, #277) from `self.num_scans`, the
component count of the current SOS. `decode_into` restores the SOS
parameters of the scan the checkpoint was saved in, so an incremental decode
that resumed inside a later scan listing all components took the row-by-row
path: it dropped the buffered planes of the earlier scans and rendered from
the current scan alone ("incremental pixels diverge from one-shot decode",
e.g. a constant third channel). Decide from the first SOS of the image
(`ScanDecodeState::sos_snapshot`, new helper
`first_scan_has_all_components`); one-shot decodes are unchanged. This was
the cause of 38 of the 40 incremental/one-shot mismatches that remained after
the other incremental fixes, across all their messages ("Unknown marker in
bit stream", "Unexpected marker ... at restart boundary", "SOS after a
baseline scan that already had all components", "Bad Huffman Code", "AC
coefficient run past the end of the block", scan exhausted). Includes a
regression test (tests/incremental_resume.rs).

Not fixed upstream as of zune-image 2cdbbf5.
Upstream: open #506 (recover sequential component scans, "used the wrong
scan geometry") reworks the same multi-scan path; no issue for the resume.

diff --git a/crates/zune-jpeg/src/decoder.rs b/crates/zune-jpeg/src/decoder.rs
index ef514de6..c685741b 100644
--- a/crates/zune-jpeg/src/decoder.rs
+++ b/crates/zune-jpeg/src/decoder.rs
@@ -1967,6 +1967,19 @@ where
         })
     }
 
+    /// Whether the first scan of the image carries every component, i.e. the
+    /// baseline image is decoded row by row rather than buffered until all
+    /// component scans are in. Resuming from a checkpoint in a later scan
+    /// restores that scan's SOS parameters, so the current `num_scans` does not
+    /// answer this.
+    pub(crate) fn first_scan_has_all_components(&self) -> bool {
+        let num_scans = self
+            .scan_state
+            .as_deref()
+            .map_or(self.num_scans, |state| state.sos_snapshot.num_scans);
+        usize::from(num_scans) == self.components.len()
+    }
+
     pub(crate) fn baseline_scans_seen(&self) -> usize {
         self.scan_state.as_deref().map_or(0, |state| state.baseline_scans_seen)
     }
